WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:16.474
Could you see that?

00:00:17.308 --> 00:00:17.767
Yeah.

00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:19.853
Come together.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.146
There's a logical explanation.

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:22.146
It's a ghost.

00:00:22.146 --> 00:00:23.148
What?

00:00:23.898 --> 00:00:26.860
So we're dealing with a, 
uh...

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.194
Ghostwriter?

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:33.575
My pocket watch has stopped.

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:35.410
If you don't mind I'd 
appreciate the time.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.662
There's a talking rabbit 
that nobody can see but us.

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:40.290
I think the ghost who was 
sending us messages 

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.833
also sent us the rabbit.

00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:45.545
This way.

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:49.507
You're gonna think 
this is bizarre,

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:51.259
but what if your 
grandma is Ghostwriter?

00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:53.011
She did bring us all together.

00:00:53.011 --> 00:00:54.929
Grandpa said even though 
grandma's gone

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:56.014
she’ll always be with us.

00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:59.517
Your grandma had 
this old letter. 

00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:01.227
She even kept it in a fancy box.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.228
Secret letter?

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:04.898
Did y'all say you need 
help finding something?

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.941
‘Cause I'm real good 
at finding stuff.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.072
I don't think grandma 
wanted anyone to find this.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.656
Until now.

00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:15.283
The letter was signed “S."

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.035
Who's “S”?

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:20.955
What was that?

00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:22.499
A clue from Ghostwriter.

00:01:22.499 --> 00:01:23.583
Follow what?

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:25.210
Follow the money.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:27.712
A check?

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:28.712
If we can see the
signature

00:01:28.712 --> 00:01:30.215
we'll know if that guy is “S."

00:01:30.215 --> 00:01:31.382
You knew Ruben's grandma?

00:01:31.382 --> 00:01:35.345
She was sure that 
this bookstore was haunted.

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:37.430
So if your grandma knew 

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.890
there was a ghost
in the bookstore...

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.935
Then maybe she's not the ghost.

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:45.480
Woah.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.689
GW's painting.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.693
Cobalt Mask?

00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:52.403
There's no author in here.

00:01:52.403 --> 00:01:53.696
That's a first.

00:01:56.741 --> 00:01:58.284
This is gonna be interesting.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.745
Rumor has it
there's an unpublished

00:02:00.745 --> 00:02:02.372
Mason Briggs manuscript.

00:02:03.206 --> 00:02:04.249
That's Ghostwriter.

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:05.083
He's back.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.544
Maybe it's the 
number of the storage unit.

00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:13.049
This must be the typewriter 
he used to write the manuscript.

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:14.801
What else can be 
written on a typewriter?

00:02:16.594 --> 00:02:17.262
A secret letter?

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.558
Mason Briggs wrote this 
letter to my grandma.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.395
Mason Briggs is a made-up name.

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:26.271
You are correct.

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:28.022
Mason Briggs is a pseudonym.

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:31.693
I can't believe we hit 
another dead end.

00:02:34.946 --> 00:02:36.948
Ew, don't touch random 
things on the subway.

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:41.244
Check it out.

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:42.996
This newspaper's 
from the future.

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:50.044
Everything in this book 
has built to this moment.

00:02:51.296 --> 00:02:53.089
High stakes
and full of suspense.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:56.885
Can you believe GW's 

00:02:56.885 --> 00:02:58.887
sending us on a 
time travel mystery?

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.514
Yes, I can.

